IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part X, sections 106 and 107 -- THE FIRST
-- DIRECTORS, THE ELECTION OF DIRECTORS AND THEIR TERMS, APPOINTMENT OF ADDITIONAL DIRECTORS, AND CUMULATIVE
-- VOTING. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. Where a provision says what follows in
-- a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within this module a rule that depends on a sibling calls it and takes its inputs. "Prescribed" facts are
-- plain inputs (the regulations are not among the sources). The keel's input name is used for the
-- corporation being a distributing corporation.

§ `s 106 Election and appointment of directors`

§§ `s 106(1) Notice of directors`

-- src:1248 | Notice of directors
-- src:1249 | 106 (1) At the time of sending articles of incorporation, the incorporators shall send to the Director a notice of directors in the form that the Director fixes, and the Director shall file the notice.
@ref CBCA s 106(1) (src:1248-1249)
GIVEN `the notice of directors is sent at the time of sending the articles of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in the form that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the incorporators have sent the notice of directors as required within s 106(1)` MEANS
        `the notice of directors is sent at the time of sending the articles of incorporation`
    AND `the notice is in the form that the Director fixes`

-- src:1248 | Notice of directors
-- src:1249 | 106 (1) At the time of sending articles of incorporation, the incorporators shall send to the Director a notice of directors in the form that the Director fixes, and the Director shall file the notice.
@ref CBCA s 106(1) (src:1248-1249)
GIVEN `the Director has received the notice of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must file the notice of directors within s 106(1)` MEANS
    `the Director has received the notice of directors`

§§ `s 106(2) Term of office`

-- "From the issue of the certificate of incorporation until the first meeting of shareholders": the director
-- holds office from the day the certificate issues through the day of that meeting (fork F-P10-3).
-- src:1250 | Term of office
-- src:1251 | (2) Each director named in the notice referred to in subsection (1) holds office from the issue of the certificate of incorporation until the first meeting of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 106(2) (src:1250-1251)
GIVEN `the director is named in the notice of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the certificate of incorporation was issued` IS A DATE
      `the date of the first meeting of shareholders, if it has been held` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director named in the notice holds office on the day asked about within s 106(2)` MEANS
        `the director is named in the notice of directors`
    AND `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date the certificate of incorporation was issued`
    AND CONSIDER `the date of the first meeting of shareholders, if it has been held`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST m THEN `the day asked about` AT MOST m

§§ `s 106(3) Election of directors`

-- src:1252 | Election of directors
-- src:1253 | (3) Subject to subsection (3.1) and paragraph 107(b), shareholders of a corporation shall, by ordinary resolution at the first meeting of shareholders and at each succeeding annual meeting at which an election of directors is required, elect directors to hold office for a term ending not later than the close of the third annual meeting of shareholders following the election.
@ref CBCA s 106(3) (src:1252-1253)
GIVEN `the meeting is the first meeting of shareholders or an annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an election of directors is required at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders must elect directors by ordinary resolution within s 106(3)` MEANS
        `the meeting is the first meeting of shareholders or an annual meeting`
    AND `an election of directors is required at the meeting`

-- The term "ending not later than the close of the third annual meeting of shareholders following the
-- election" (3); "the close of the next annual meeting" for a distributing corporation (3.1), unless it is
-- in a prescribed class or circumstance (3.2), when (3) applies again; and cumulative voting always gives one
-- (s 107(f), "the close of the first annual meeting following the director's election"). The answer is the
-- number of annual meetings following the election, at the close of the last of which the term must end.
-- src:1252 | Election of directors
-- src:1253 | (3) Subject to subsection (3.1) and paragraph 107(b), shareholders of a corporation shall, by ordinary resolution at the first meeting of shareholders and at each succeeding annual meeting at which an election of directors is required, elect directors to hold office for a term ending not later than the close of the third annual meeting of shareholders following the election.
-- src:1254 | Election of directors — distributing corporations
-- src:1255 | (3.1) Subject to paragraph 107(b), shareholders of a distributing corporation shall, by ordinary resolution at the first meeting of shareholders and at each succeeding annual meeting at which an election of directors is required, elect directors to hold office for a term ending not later than the close of the next annual meeting of shareholders following the election.
-- src:1256 | Exceptions — certain distributing corporations
-- src:1257 | (3.2) Despite subsection (3.1), in the case of any prescribed class of distributing corporations or in any prescribed circumstances respecting distributing corporations or classes of distributing corporations, the directors are to be elected in accordance with subsection (3).
@ref CBCA s 106(3) (src:1252-1257)
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is in a class of distributing corporations or in circumstances prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the latest annual meeting at whose close a director's term may end within s 106(3)` MEANS
    IF     `a director ceases to hold office at the close of the first annual meeting following election within s 107(f)`
               `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
        OR (    `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
            AND (NOT `the corporation is in a class of distributing corporations or in circumstances prescribed by the regulations`))
    THEN 1
    ELSE 3

§§ `s 106(3.3) Separate vote for each candidate`

-- src:1258 | Separate vote for each candidate
-- src:1259 | (3.3) If the election of directors is for a prescribed corporation, a separate vote of shareholders shall be taken with respect to each candidate nominated for director.
@ref CBCA s 106(3.3) (src:1258-1259)
GIVEN `the election of directors is for a corporation prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a separate vote must be taken for each candidate within s 106(3.3)` MEANS
    `the election of directors is for a corporation prescribed by the regulations`

§§ `s 106(3.4) Majority voting`

-- NOTHING: the corporation is not a distributing corporation, or is in a prescribed class, or there is more
-- than one candidate for a position, so s 106(3.4) says nothing. "Unless the articles require a greater number
-- of votes": read as a number of votes in favour the articles require, if more than a majority (fork F-P10-4).
-- src:1260 | Majority voting
-- src:1261 | (3.4) If, at a meeting of shareholders of a distributing corporation — other than in the case of a prescribed class of distributing corporations — at which an election of directors is required, there is only one candidate nominated for each position available on the board, each candidate is elected only if the number of votes cast in their favour represents a majority of the votes cast for and against them by the shareholders who are present in person or represented by proxy, unless the articles require a greater number of votes.
@ref CBCA s 106(3.4) (src:1260-1261)
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is in a class of distributing corporations prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is only one candidate nominated for each position available on the board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes cast in favour of the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER
      `the votes cast against the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes in favour that the articles require, if they require a greater number than a majority` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the candidate receives the majority needed to be elected within s 106(3.4)` MEANS
    IF     `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
       AND (NOT `the corporation is in a class of distributing corporations prescribed by the regulations`)
       AND `there is only one candidate nominated for each position available on the board`
    THEN JUST (    `the votes cast in favour of the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy`
                       GREATER THAN `the votes cast against the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy`
               AND CONSIDER `the number of votes in favour that the articles require, if they require a greater number than a majority`
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                   WHEN JUST required THEN `the votes cast in favour of the candidate by shareholders present in person or represented by proxy` AT LEAST required)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 106(4) Staggered terms`

-- NOTHING: no directors are elected at a meeting, so s 106(4) says nothing.
-- src:1262 | Staggered terms
-- src:1263 | (4) It is not necessary that all directors elected at a meeting of shareholders hold office for the same term.
@ref CBCA s 106(4) (src:1262-1263)
GIVEN `directors are elected at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`all directors elected at the meeting must hold office for the same term within s 106(4)` MEANS
    IF `directors are elected at a meeting of shareholders`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 106(5) No stated terms`

-- NOTHING: the director was elected for an expressly stated term, so s 106(5) says nothing.
-- src:1264 | No stated terms
-- src:1265 | (5) A director not elected for an expressly stated term ceases to hold office at the close of the first annual meeting of shareholders following the director’s election.
@ref CBCA s 106(5) (src:1264-1265)
GIVEN `the director was elected for an expressly stated term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the close of the first annual meeting of shareholders following the election` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the director still holds office on the day asked about within s 106(5)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the director was elected for an expressly stated term`
    THEN JUST (`the day asked about` AT MOST `the date of the close of the first annual meeting of shareholders following the election`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 106(6.1) Incumbent director not elected`

-- The director may continue in office until the earlier of the 90th day after the day of the election and the
-- day their successor is appointed or elected.
-- src:1268 | Incumbent director not elected
-- src:1269 | (6.1) If an incumbent director who was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection (3.4) was not elected during the election, the director may continue in office until the earlier of
-- src:1270 | (a) the 90th day after the day of the election; and
-- src:1271 | (b) the day on which their successor is appointed or elected.
@ref CBCA s 106(6.1) (src:1268-1271)
GIVEN `the incumbent director was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the election` IS A DATE
      `the day on which their successor is appointed or elected, if one has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the incumbent director who was not elected may continue in office on the day asked about within s 106(6.1)` MEANS
        `the incumbent director was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected`
    AND `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the day of the election`
    AND `the day asked about` AT MOST (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 90, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the day of the election`)
    AND CONSIDER `the day on which their successor is appointed or elected, if one has been`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST s THEN `the day asked about` AT MOST s

§§ `s 106(6) Incumbent directors`

-- src:1266 | Incumbent directors
-- src:1267 | (6) Despite subsections (2), (3) to (3.2) and (5) and subject to subsection (6.1), if directors are not elected at a meeting of shareholders, the incumbent directors continue in office until their successors are elected.
@ref CBCA s 106(6) (src:1266-1267)
GIVEN `directors are not elected at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director is an incumbent director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `their successors have been elected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the incumbent director was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the incumbent director continues in office within s 106(6)` MEANS
        `directors are not elected at a meeting of shareholders`
    AND `the director is an incumbent director`
    AND (NOT `their successors have been elected`)
    AND (NOT `the incumbent director was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected`)

§§ `s 106(7) Vacancy`

-- src:1272 | Vacancy
-- src:1273 | (7) If, for either of the following reasons, a meeting of shareholders fails to elect the number or the minimum number of directors required by the articles, the directors elected at that meeting may exercise all the powers of the directors if the number of directors so elected constitutes a quorum:
-- src:1274 | (a) a lack of consent, disqualification under subsection 105(1) or the death of any candidates; or
-- src:1275 | (b) a lack of a majority referred to in subsection (3.4).
@ref CBCA s 106(7) (src:1272-1275)
GIVEN `the meeting fails to elect the number or the minimum number of directors required by the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is due to a lack of consent, disqualification under subsection 105(1) or the death of any candidates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is due to a lack of a majority referred to in subsection 106(3.4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors so elected constitutes a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors elected may exercise all the powers of the directors within s 106(7)` MEANS
        `the meeting fails to elect the number or the minimum number of directors required by the articles`
    AND (   `the failure is due to a lack of consent, disqualification under subsection 105(1) or the death of any candidates`
         OR `the failure is due to a lack of a majority referred to in subsection 106(3.4)`)
    AND `the number of directors so elected constitutes a quorum`

§§ `s 106(8) Appointment of directors`

-- The total number of additional directors appointed may not exceed one third of the number of directors
-- elected at the previous annual meeting.
-- src:1276 | Appointment of directors
-- src:1277 | (8) The directors may, unless the articles otherwise provide, appoint one or more additional directors, who shall hold office for a term ending not later than the close of the next annual meeting of shareholders, but the total number of directors so appointed shall not exceed one third of the number of directors elected at the previous annual meeting of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 106(8) (src:1276-1277)
GIVEN `the articles otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of directors elected at the previous annual meeting of shareholders` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of additional directors already appointed under subsection 106(8)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of additional directors proposed to be appointed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may appoint the additional directors within s 106(8)` MEANS
        (NOT `the articles otherwise provide`)
    AND (`the number of additional directors already appointed under subsection 106(8)` PLUS `the number of additional directors proposed to be appointed`)
            AT MOST (`the number of directors elected at the previous annual meeting of shareholders` DIVIDED BY 3)

-- src:1276 | Appointment of directors
-- src:1277 | (8) The directors may, unless the articles otherwise provide, appoint one or more additional directors, who shall hold office for a term ending not later than the close of the next annual meeting of shareholders, but the total number of directors so appointed shall not exceed one third of the number of directors elected at the previous annual meeting of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 106(8) (src:1276-1277)
GIVEN `the date of the close of the next annual meeting of shareholders` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the additional director may hold office on the day asked about within s 106(8)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT MOST `the date of the close of the next annual meeting of shareholders`

§§ `s 106(8.1) Exception`

-- NOTHING: the individual was not a candidate in a s 106(3.4) election who failed to be elected, so s 106(8.1)
-- says nothing.
-- src:1278 | Exception
-- src:1279 | (8.1) If an individual who was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection (3.4) was not elected during that election, the individual is not to be appointed, except in prescribed circumstances, as a director under subsection (8) or 111(1) before the next meeting of shareholders at which an election of directors is required.
@ref CBCA s 106(8.1) (src:1278-1279)
GIVEN `the individual was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is in circumstances prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the next meeting of shareholders at which an election of directors is required has been held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the individual may be appointed as a director under subsection 106(8) or 111(1) within s 106(8.1)` MEANS
    IF `the individual was a candidate in an election held in accordance with subsection 106(3.4) and was not elected`
    THEN JUST (   `the appointment is in circumstances prescribed by the regulations`
               OR `the next meeting of shareholders at which an election of directors is required has been held`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 106(9) Election or appointment as director`

-- (b)(i): consented in writing before the election or appointment, or within ten days after it.
-- src:1280 | Election or appointment as director
-- src:1281 | (9) An individual who is elected or appointed to hold office as a director is not a director and is deemed not to have been elected or appointed to hold office as a director unless
-- src:1282 | (a) he or she was present at the meeting when the election or appointment took place and he or she did not refuse to hold office as a director; or
-- src:1283 | (b) he or she was not present at the meeting when the election or appointment took place and
-- src:1284 | (i) he or she consented to hold office as a director in writing before the election or appointment or within ten days after it, or
-- src:1285 | (ii) he or she has acted as a director pursuant to the election or appointment.
@ref CBCA s 106(9) (src:1280-1285)
GIVEN `the individual was present at the meeting when the election or appointment took place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual refused to hold office as a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the election or appointment` IS A DATE
      `the date the individual consented in writing to hold office as a director, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the individual has acted as a director pursuant to the election or appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the individual is a director within s 106(9)` MEANS
        (    `the individual was present at the meeting when the election or appointment took place`
         AND (NOT `the individual refused to hold office as a director`))
    OR  (    (NOT `the individual was present at the meeting when the election or appointment took place`)
         AND (   CONSIDER `the date the individual consented in writing to hold office as a director, if they did`
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                 WHEN JUST c THEN c AT MOST (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 10, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`) `counted from` `the date of the election or appointment`)
              OR `the individual has acted as a director pursuant to the election or appointment`))

§ `s 107 Cumulative voting`

-- Each rule asks whether the articles provide for cumulative voting; where they do not, s 107 says nothing.
§§ `s 107(a)`

-- src:1287 | 107 Where the articles provide for cumulative voting,
-- src:1288 | (a) the articles shall require a fixed number and not a minimum and maximum number of directors;
@ref CBCA s 107(a) (src:1287 src:1288)
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles require a fixed number and not a minimum and maximum number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles meet the requirement for a fixed number of directors within s 107(a)` MEANS
        (NOT `the articles provide for cumulative voting`)
    OR  `the articles require a fixed number and not a minimum and maximum number of directors`

§§ `s 107(b)`

-- The shareholder may cast the votes attached to their shares multiplied by the number of directors to be
-- elected, all for one candidate or distributed among the candidates as they like.
-- src:1287 | 107 Where the articles provide for cumulative voting,
-- src:1289 | (b) each shareholder entitled to vote at an election of directors has the right to cast a number of votes equal to the number of votes attached to the shares held by the shareholder multiplied by the number of directors to be elected, and may cast all of those votes in favour of one candidate or distribute them among the candidates in any manner;
@ref CBCA s 107(b) (src:1287 src:1289)
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes attached to the shares held by the shareholder` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors to be elected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of votes the shareholder may cast within s 107(b)` MEANS
    IF `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
    THEN JUST (`the number of votes attached to the shares held by the shareholder` TIMES `the number of directors to be elected`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "May cast all of those votes in favour of one candidate or distribute them among the candidates in any
-- manner": a distribution is permitted when no candidate gets a negative number and the total does not exceed
-- the votes the shareholder may cast.
-- src:1287 | 107 Where the articles provide for cumulative voting,
-- src:1289 | (b) each shareholder entitled to vote at an election of directors has the right to cast a number of votes equal to the number of votes attached to the shares held by the shareholder multiplied by the number of directors to be elected, and may cast all of those votes in favour of one candidate or distribute them among the candidates in any manner;
@ref CBCA s 107(b) (src:1287 src:1289)
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes the shareholder may cast` IS A NUMBER
      `the votes given to each candidate` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholder's distribution of votes is permitted within s 107(b)` MEANS
        `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
    AND all (GIVEN v YIELD v AT LEAST 0) `the votes given to each candidate`
    AND sum `the votes given to each candidate` AT MOST `the number of votes the shareholder may cast`

§§ `s 107(c)`

-- src:1287 | 107 Where the articles provide for cumulative voting,
-- src:1290 | (c) a separate vote of shareholders shall be taken with respect to each candidate nominated for director unless a resolution is passed unanimously permitting two or more persons to be elected by a single resolution;
@ref CBCA s 107(c) (src:1287 src:1290)
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a resolution is passed unanimously permitting two or more persons to be elected by a single resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a separate vote must be taken for each candidate within s 107(c)` MEANS
        `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
    AND (NOT `a resolution is passed unanimously permitting two or more persons to be elected by a single resolution`)

§§ `s 107(d)`

-- The shareholder who voted for more than one candidate without specifying the distribution is deemed to
-- have distributed the votes equally among them: the answer is the votes each candidate receives from them.
-- src:1287 | 107 Where the articles provide for cumulative voting,
-- src:1291 | (d) if a shareholder has voted for more than one candidate without specifying the distribution of votes, the shareholder is deemed to have distributed the votes equally among those candidates;
@ref CBCA s 107(d) (src:1287 src:1291)
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of candidates the shareholder voted for` IS A NUMBER
      `the shareholder specified the distribution of votes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes the shareholder cast` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the votes each candidate receives from the shareholder within s 107(d)` MEANS
    IF     `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
       AND `the number of candidates the shareholder voted for` GREATER THAN 1
       AND (NOT `the shareholder specified the distribution of votes`)
    THEN JUST (`the number of votes the shareholder cast` DIVIDED BY `the number of candidates the shareholder voted for`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 107(e)`

-- The candidates who receive the least votes are eliminated until the number remaining equals the number of
-- positions: the answer is how many are eliminated. NOTHING: the number of candidates does not exceed the
-- number of positions.
-- src:1287 | 107 Where the articles provide for cumulative voting,
-- src:1292 | (e) if the number of candidates nominated for director exceeds the number of positions to be filled, the candidates who receive the least number of votes shall be eliminated until the number of candidates remaining equals the number of positions to be filled;
@ref CBCA s 107(e) (src:1287 src:1292)
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of candidates nominated for director` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of positions to be filled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of candidates to be eliminated within s 107(e)` MEANS
    IF     `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
       AND `the number of candidates nominated for director` GREATER THAN `the number of positions to be filled`
    THEN JUST (`the number of candidates nominated for director` MINUS `the number of positions to be filled`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 107(f)`

-- src:1287 | 107 Where the articles provide for cumulative voting,
-- src:1293 | (f) each director ceases to hold office at the close of the first annual meeting of shareholders following the director’s election;
@ref CBCA s 107(f) (src:1287 src:1293)
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a director ceases to hold office at the close of the first annual meeting following election within s 107(f)` MEANS
    `the articles provide for cumulative voting`

§§ `s 107(g)`

-- NOTHING: the articles do not provide for cumulative voting.
-- src:1287 | 107 Where the articles provide for cumulative voting,
-- src:1294 | (g) a director may be removed from office only if the number of votes cast in favour of the director’s removal is greater than the product of the number of directors required by the articles and the number of votes cast against the motion; and
@ref CBCA s 107(g) (src:1287 src:1294)
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes cast in favour of the director's removal` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes cast against the motion` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors required by the articles` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the vote needed to remove the director is met within s 107(g)` MEANS
    IF `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
    THEN JUST (`the number of votes cast in favour of the director's removal` GREATER THAN (`the number of directors required by the articles` TIMES `the number of votes cast against the motion`))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 107(h)`

-- NOTHING: the articles do not provide for cumulative voting.
-- src:1287 | 107 Where the articles provide for cumulative voting,
-- src:1295 | (h) the number of directors required by the articles may be decreased only if the votes cast in favour of the motion to decrease the number of directors is greater than the product of the number of directors required by the articles and the number of votes cast against the motion.
@ref CBCA s 107(h) (src:1287 src:1295)
GIVEN `the articles provide for cumulative voting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the votes cast in favour of the motion to decrease the number of directors` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes cast against the motion` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors required by the articles` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the vote needed to decrease the number of directors is met within s 107(h)` MEANS
    IF `the articles provide for cumulative voting`
    THEN JUST (`the votes cast in favour of the motion to decrease the number of directors` GREATER THAN (`the number of directors required by the articles` TIMES `the number of votes cast against the motion`))
    ELSE NOTHING
